      "created_at": "2022-01-04T22:12:41.418Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I don’t think it’s really in flavor for Greazer to be flipping people off; he’s loosely based on Lobo, but Lobo is a gritty 80s bad-attitude-dude, while Greazer is a groady sleazeball from the 50s.  “The Bird” is much more appropriate enough for the first one than the second, given that the idea of “bad language” and similar concepts loomed much larger in the older decade.</p>",
